comments[28]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T13:43:47.071Z",codex-sol,"Fleet CI v2; companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Reuse the existing hung Bun gate item. Preserve required test (22) and test (26), generated-package acceptance, committed build-output checks, strict tracker health, privacy and release verifiers. Split quick hosted PR gates from exhaustive local deep gates; add bounded jobs and deterministic test depth. No release workflow or verifier changes."
  "2026-11-15T13:47:57.883Z",codex-sol,"Latest successful main run 43691008662: Node 22 npm/Bun gates 59m04s/58m43s; Node 26 75m10s/76m10s. gh run view --log returned empty; individual jobs API log supplied timings: seeded property 693.34s, discovery 636.63s, compiler matrix 505.66s, packed acceptance 269.96s. Quick retains deterministic prefixes and unchanged coverage thresholds; full remains deep. Generated projects inherit adapted workflows and the helper and now execute their own release gate under both installed graphs. Bun project paths are accepted; bunx is a separate local-bin smoke. The historical Bun handle leak is contained, not diagnosed as fixed."
  "2026-11-15T13:50:43.690Z",codex-sol,"Deep uses four Node/runtime matrix legs, each with a fresh installer graph and its own 120-minute ceiling. This preserves all four full gates without stacking the measured 75-minute npm and 76-minute Bun gates in one 120-minute job. No coverage/source threshold changes."
  "2026-11-15T13:51:15.430Z",codex-sol,"Pre-push checks: typecheck, test compilation, lint, build, duplicate gate (0%), docstrings and changelog pass. Strict health passes with inherited advisories. Strict YAML parser passes six source/generated workflows; actionlint is unavailable. Focused generator-asset, graph-failure and depth regressions pass (15 tests). Quick touched-file batch is running with a 20-minute bound; no full local run is planned. Coverage remains a required quick PR gate at the unchanged 100/100/100 thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T13:57:34.874Z",codex-sol,Harness scale validation also rejects budgets above the portable signed 32-bit timer ceiling; positive fractional scales round upward. This prevents huge scale values from overflowing or becoming immediate timers. Depth and deep-graph invariants pass 3/3 after the guard.
  "2026-11-15T13:59:24.938Z",codex-sol,"Final generated-package/deep-graph/depth batch: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 node --test test/backend.test.ts test/ci-consumer-graphs.test.ts test/depth.test.ts passes 29/29, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 124.37 seconds linked-command wall. This executes both generated installer graphs and their own release gates. A later timer-overflow guard passes the separate 3-test depth/deep smoke. Broad quick touched-file batch is still bounded to 1200 seconds."
  "2026-11-15T14:08:30.808Z",codex-sol,"Broad quick touched-file run stopped at its 1200-second harness budget: 235 passing tests, one obsolete generated-Bun audit failure, three cancelled suites. That run loaded the pre-fix generator: npm audit rejected the Bun graph because it had no npm lockfile (ENOLOCK). The committed generator now creates an audit lockfile; the fresh final generator/deep/depth batch passes 29/29 in 124.37 seconds. Remaining compiler suites are incomplete on this overloaded host; this is not a successful complete quick run. No full local depth or full quick coverage was attempted. PR CI run 43721246259 had both required checks queued at the snapshot; no completed created-to-completed wall time exists. CodeQL run 43721246139 was also queued. Final typecheck, test compilation, lint, integer-timer tests and bunx compiler smoke pass. Coverage, total quick duration and deep capacity remain unverified; no release files, variables, protection or review threads changed."
  "2026-11-15T19:58:36.596Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D: verify PR 217 findings, preserve documentation validation and privacy checks, make generated private runners opt-in, scale harness timeout fixture lifetime, and diagnose both 30-minute required-check cancellations using individual job logs. Review all six CI defect classes."
  "2026-11-15T20:09:12.701Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D: all four review findings are valid. Generated and root deep workflows default to hosted Ubuntu unless PM_LOCAL_DEEP=on; generated deep jobs now separate Node x npm/Bun gates and actions are pinned. Docs tier keeps identity/privacy plus README package links, compatibility-floor and focused SDK compiler documentation tests. Harness timeout lifetime scales at 1.5 and 20; invalid scale is checked before spawn. Self-review restored executable tracker CodeQL eligibility and skips native invalid filename corpora on win32. No covered implementation source changed this round; coverage is not repeated. Required checks on prior head cancelled at 30 minutes immediately before the unbounded overlapping-peer test; its peer now has an integer scaled hard-kill timeout and explicit result exit. Focused regression is running; final CI recovery remains unverified."
  "2026-11-15T20:20:02.490Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D final local results on Node 24.19.0: typecheck/build:test/lint pass (23.41 s final); workflow/depth/metadata/compatibility/release/identity batch 28 passed (7.33 s), including strict root/generated YAML; focused compiler documentation 1 passed (4.94 s); backend deadline/invalid-scale/clean-network-env regressions 3 passed (10.57 s final). Full backend/consumer-graph/depth batch passed 29 (329.65 s) before the final added invalid-scale case, which passed separately. POSIX API/path corpora passed 17 with no skips (713.78 s). Overlapping caller contract passed all six phases and observer cleanup at scale 3 (465.40 s); initial scale-1 60-second peer watchdog failed under host load (283.86 s overall) and is retained as failed diagnostic evidence, not approval. Changelog regeneration/check and strict source tracker health passed (49.34 s linked command). The 30-minute prior hosted cancellations are traced to the previously unbounded peer test; its bound/explicit result exit improves failure containment, while hosted recovery and the general Bun handle issue remain unverified. All four finding thread IDs fixed: PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63qKb7, PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63qkY_, PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63qKb8, PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63qkZB. No source coverage change or local coverage run this round; full depth and replacement-head CI remain unverified. No item closure or thread action."
  "2026-11-15T22:24:21.409Z",codex-sol,"Round E: verified assigned review findings and current checks. Fix valid portability, gate-order and timeout regressions; preserve product deadlines, privacy/identity and self-host gates. Run targeted quick tests and required tooling checks before an explicit-path commit. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T22:37:46.091Z",codex-sol,"Round E evidence: PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63udS7 is valid: generated deep Bun legs never called test:bun. Add that explicit behavioral gate and ordering regression. Both failing checks actually reached the 30-minute job limit; the logs stop before the overlapping caller-boundary test finishes. Retain all six competition phases using a small actual compiled SDK fixture rather than repeated copies of the full published SDK dependency graph; validate the targeted case."
  "2026-11-15T22:45:13.561Z",codex-sol,"Round E direct targeted check: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 node --test --test-name-pattern=\"each overlapping caller boundary\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts; passed: 1 test, all six boundaries, 342352 ms. No package coverage sources were changed; no package coverage run was performed."
  "2026-11-15T22:50:05.287Z",codex-sol,"Round E final verification: typecheck, lint (docstring gate where no lint script exists), touched regression tests, workflow/tooling tests, strict workflow YAML and changelog:check passed. Duplication gates passed where provided. Self-review retained docs/tracker privacy and identity checks, unscaled product deadlines, integer-rounded validated harness budgets, platform filename guards and generated-only quick thresholds. No package coverage sources were edited; no package coverage run. No review thread actions or merge. Shared-runner hold and SteveBot commit identity will be checked before push. Hosted CI is intentionally not awaited. The targeted six-phase compiler competition check passed 1/1 in 342352 ms. Hosted timeout improvement remains to be measured after push."
  "2026-11-16T00:22:55.542Z",codex-sol,"Round F: verify assigned review findings and failing Actions checks, audit related tier contracts, add regressions, run focused gates and push without waiting for CI. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-16T00:35:36.582Z",codex-sol,"Round F: PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63vZMz is valid. Run 43771856126 spent 29m56s in the Node 26 release gate and 29m59s in Node 22 tests; setup completed under 20s. Preserve all six tracker competitions with one minimal peer compiler matrix in quick; exhaustive repeated matrices and all four packed installer/bound lanes remain deep. PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM63vZM4 is valid; 25 deterministic samples now include all three extensions and nine syntax forms. Self-review restores local-by-default deep runners in root and shipped workflows. Tooling tests, typecheck, lint and strict YAML pass; touched compiler tests are running."
  "2026-11-16T01:20:36.010Z",codex-sol,"All assertions in the broad SDK file completed successfully at quick depth, including 25 generated dependency graphs, 188 edges and 50 matching checker rows. A diagnostic inspector evaluation injected a dynamic-import rejection into that test process, making the process result invalid as a clean gate. Repeat the SDK file without instrumentation; the separate program-graph checks continue. This is a validation-process error, not a source finding."
  "2026-11-16T01:23:14.844Z",codex-sol,"Use a clean focused rerun of all SDK cases affected by the changed overlap fixture, packed lane selection, minimal consumer helper and dependency worker, plus both real 25-case program matrices. The broad run already completed unchanged assertions; its process-level diagnostic rejection is recorded separately. Restore the unrelated explicit compiler regression configuration to minimize the final diff."
  "2026-11-16T01:40:20.445Z",codex-sol,"Clean final quick-depth verification passed all 19 focused SDK/program tests in about 970 seconds, without instrumentation. This covers every changed SDK fixture/helper/worker case and both real TypeScript 5.9.3 and 6.0.3 matrices: 25 combinations each, all three extensions and nine syntax forms. The 17 PM-linked workflow/depth/release tests also passed. Final typecheck, lint, test compilation, strict YAML, changelog and author-email checks passed. No coverage source changed, so no local coverage was run. Both review findings are fixed; exhaustive packed lanes and repeated peer matrices remain deep. Hosted job timing and full coverage await orchestrator CI verification; keep the item open."
  "2026-11-16T02:22:42.880Z",codex-sol,"Quick-fit follow-up: cancelled required checks reached the unchanged 30-minute ceiling without a test failure. Audit exhaustive boundary, compiler and consumer matrices; retain deterministic kind coverage in quick and complete enumeration in deep. Compare focused local quick timings, then measure PR job steps within the 30-minute post-push observation window. Product timing contracts and coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-16T02:29:37.514Z",codex-sol,"Finite quick selection now preserves 9 compiler dimension representatives (both runtime kinds and SDK bounds), all 16 hostile specifier kinds across alternating locations, 18 discovery kinds, each supplementary flag, one compiler per structural family and one packed npm/current SDK path. Deep retains every original combination. Typecheck, test compilation, lint and depth-helper tests pass. Frozen baseline and revised quick touched-file runs are in progress; shared-host timings are comparative, not hosted-runner guarantees."
  "2026-11-16T02:31:57.013Z",codex-sol,"Validation before the early push: npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run lint; npm run build; PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --test test/depth.test.ts all pass. The helper also passes through pm test --run --only-last --progress (4 tests). Frozen old-depth baseline and the linked revised touched-file command continue in parallel; measurements will follow. Coverage thresholds and all product deadlines are unchanged. Do not interpret pending focused tests or CI as approval."
  "2026-11-16T03:02:05.668Z",codex-sol,"Bounded quick-fit evidence for code head fa7d363: the 15-minute target is NOT met. Both Linux checks remain running after more than 28 minutes; their test-step lower bounds and every completed setup step are in the Jobs API table below. GitHub returns 404 for unfinished job logs, so a new complete per-test CI ranking is unavailable. Unchanged next candidates from prior logs: post-compile isolation 103.822s, malformed API results 101.273s, import mutations 50.837-70.221s, SDK-bound declaration pairs 51.122s and location tripwires 47.373s. Local quick validation ended at the time budget: 20 passed, zero assertion failures, one cancelled SDK-contracts file. The 5.9.3 structural API and 9-case 6.0.3 graph families pass; the broad suite and coverage are not certified. Local before/after and exact commands are in docs/ci-quick-fit-measurements.md. Release the claim, retain in_progress, never close.\n\n# Quick-fit measurements: pm-ts-starter\n\nCode head: `fa7d36307fb34c30a45130689b32709d342339e1`. [CI run 43792754575](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/actions/runs/43792754575).\nJobs API snapshot: 2026-11-16T03:00:40+00:00. All local timing commands use `PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick`; unset/full depth is not run locally.\n\n| Job | Result at snapshot | Created to completion | Queue | Started to completion |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| test (26) | in_progress | unfinished | 2s | >= 1712s running |\n| test (22) | in_progress | unfinished | 2s | >= 1712s running |\n\nStep times are completed wall times from `started_at` to `completed_at`; running values are lower bounds, not completed durations.\n\n| Step | test (26) | test (22) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Set up job | 2s success | 2s success |\n| Checkout | 1s success | 2s success |\n| Detect code changes | 1s success | 0s success |\n| Setup Node.js | 6s success | 3s success |\n| Setup Bun | 2s success | 2s success |\n| Install dependencies | 4s success | 6s success |\n| Install project pm-github extension | 1s success | 2s success |\n| Verify tracked pm project health | 1s success | skipped |\n| Check documentation and tracker changes | skipped | skipped |\n| Build and verify committed output is current | 1s success | 0s success |\n| Engines floor tests | skipped | >= 1694s running |\n| Quick npm release gate | >= 1692s running | pending |\n| Bunx smoke | pending | pending |\n| Verify Bun can install the package graph | pending | pending |\n| Post Setup Bun | pending | pending |\n| Post Setup Node.js | pending | pending |\n| Post Checkout | pending | pending |"
  "2026-11-16T04:00:19.039Z",pi-glm,"Round G sharding plan, from the cancelled-run measurements: the quick suite never completes one hosted job (test 22: 389 tests in 1799 s then cancelled; test 26: 431 tests in 1797 s then cancelled, both inside the coverage run; static gates take ~10 s). Per-test totals from the logs: the quick Node 22 suite is ~2100-2400 s serial and is dominated by test/sdk-contracts.test.ts (~1381 s alone), which no file-based shard can fit under 12 min. Restructure: (1) split sdk-contracts.test.ts into a shared support module plus five part files sized from measured test durations (parts ~235-350 s each, published-bounds tests grouped to avoid repeated registry installs); (2) Node 22: non-required quick-shard matrix (5 shards, node --test --test-shard=k/5 --test-concurrency=1, PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick, same build/setup), required test (22) becomes an always()-aggregate that requires every shard success on code PRs and the docs gates otherwise; (3) Node 26: non-coverage release-gate steps in one job (they measure ~10 s), coverage run sharded 5 ways via a new --shard mode of scripts/coverage-gate.ts that writes per-shard JSON reports, plus a --merge gate that merges per-file line, branch and function hit counts (sum; covered iff any shard hit) and enforces the unchanged 100 percent thresholds plus the source-presence check on the union; fixture test proves sharded-then-merged equals unsharded on a real fixture project; required test (26) aggregates static, shards and merge. npm run coverage and npm run release:check stay intact for local/deep use. Round-robin shard assignment simulated on measured per-file times: worst shard ~460 s tests + setup, under the 12-minute projection. Risks: the eight tail files never completed any logged run (estimated 200-400 s total), so per-shard projections there are estimates; first CI run of this head will measure them."
  "2026-11-16T04:23:33.294Z",codex-sol,"Resuming the interrupted round G under the requested handoff. Reviewed the pending tracker changes. Implementing separate Node 22 shards, Node 26 coverage shards and exact hit union, plus non-coverage gates with required success aggregates. CI will provide timing and merged coverage evidence; thresholds and deep gates stay unchanged."
  "2026-11-16T04:37:55.412Z",codex-sol,"Implementation ready for hosted measurement: five Node 22 quick shards, five Node 26 coverage shards, a parallel non-coverage release gate, exact coverage merge and required test (22/26) aggregates. SDK split comparison: 42 test names before and after, no missing or added names; repaired missing helper/type imports from the interrupted split. Five focused split-file tests passed. Workflow, routing, native coverage-gate and merge fixtures passed 38/38 via pm test. Typecheck, build:test, lint, zero-duplication gate, docstrings and changelog check passed. Focused coverage of the modified gate is 100% lines/branches/functions; this is not full-suite coverage. Artifacts bind raw offsets and line/branch/function hits to source bytes and runtime version; missing/duplicate/mismatched shards fail closed. Thresholds and deep/local commands unchanged. Native merger uses a version-sensitive internal Node API, guarded by the real unsharded-equivalence fixture. Full-suite timing and merged coverage remain pending hosted CI."
  "2026-11-16T04:42:27.383Z",codex-sol,"Updated active file and test-command links after the split: removed the deleted monolithic entrypoint from linked files and replaced stored SDK contract commands with the five-part glob, preserving their timeouts. Historical evidence remains unchanged. AST comparison also confirms that all 42 complete test-call bodies are byte-identical before and after the split."
  "2026-11-16T04:44:42.958Z",codex-sol,"Additional supported-runtime validation caught a Node 22-only merger API shape: TestCoverage takes seven positional arguments there and an options object on Node 24/26. The native subprocess now selects the matching constructor shape. The unchanged equivalence fixture passes on Node 22.23.4 and Node 26.13.0; Node 26 focused gate coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. npm run build:test and npm run lint pass after the repair. Both repos strict check-only tracker health commands exit zero with pre-existing advisory stale-item/provenance warnings. Keeping the original bounded observation cutoff despite this corrective push."
